    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not just luck. luck implies a variance that might swing back. this feels different. it's like the math of my life is just... subtracting from zero. every time i try to create something, the energy goes into the void. it's more like a fundamental constant. i look at the data of my own existence and the trend line is just a straight descent. harder to fight a law of physics than just bad luck.",
